{"term":"suppose","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f091dbe4ef74cad06a","definition":"To take for granted; to conclude, with less than absolute supporting data; to believe.","example":"I suppose we all agree that this is the best solution.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["assume"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["I don't suppose","missuppose","supposable","supposal","supposedly","supposed to","supposure"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa5d22975af3978ea4","definition":"To theorize or hypothesize.","example":"Suppose that A implies B and B implies C. Then A implies C.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["assume"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["I don't suppose","missuppose","supposable","supposal","supposedly","supposed to","supposure"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c15d2c98bd855753f5","definition":"To imagine; to believe; to receive as true.","example":"How easy is a bush supposed a bear!","pos":"verb","synonyms":["arread","assume","fancy","conject","conjecture","daresay","dope","foreguess","go out on a limb","guess","guesstimate","hunch","hypothesize","hypotheticate","imagine","infer","overhope","posit","postulate","presume","reckon","speculate","suppose","surmise","suspect","take a stab at","take for granted","take something as read","theorize","ween"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["I don't suppose","missuppose","supposable","supposal","supposedly","supposed to","supposure"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e26e96fa0915e3d47e","definition":"To reckon to be, to account or esteem as.","example":"[He] keeps you from the honors of a Queene,\nBeing ſuppoſde his worthleſſe Concubine.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["arread","assume","fancy","conject","conjecture","daresay","dope","foreguess","go out on a limb","guess","guesstimate","hunch","hypothesize","hypotheticate","imagine","infer","overhope","posit","postulate","presume","reckon","speculate","suppose","surmise","suspect","take a stab at","take for granted","take something as read","theorize","ween"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["I don't suppose","missuppose","supposable","supposal","supposedly","supposed to","supposure"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:622d5adcf41fa68c30","definition":"To require to exist or to be true; to imply by the laws of thought or of nature.","example":"Purpose supposes foresight.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["arread","assume","fancy","conject","conjecture","daresay","dope","foreguess","go out on a limb","guess","guesstimate","hunch","hypothesize","hypotheticate","imagine","infer","overhope","posit","postulate","presume","reckon","speculate","suppose","surmise","suspect","take a stab at","take for granted","take something as read","theorize","ween"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["I don't suppose","missuppose","supposable","supposal","supposedly","supposed to","supposure"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9abb143b5305900afc","definition":"To put by fraud in the place of another; to substitute fraudulently.","exa